		<item>
		<title>Gligar</title>
		<link>http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/items/pokeballs/gligar</link>
		<pubDate>Tue, 31 Dec 2013 07:19:24 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[SSF2 DOJO Team]]></dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Pokeballs]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/?p=5003</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Gligar is a flying Pokémon that looks a bit like a bat. It&#8217;s aggressive, quick, and often deadly. And a cute lil&#8217; guy, to boot. Gligar will repeatedly charge at an opponent at lightning speed from random angles, hitting them away in the process. Each time it charges, its attack increases in strength! A solid [&#8230;]]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a href="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/Gligar.png"><img class="size-full wp-image-3835 aligncenter" alt="Gligar" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/Gligar.png" /></a></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Gligar is a flying Pokémon that looks a bit like a bat. It&#8217;s aggressive, quick, and often deadly.</p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/gligar1.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>And a cute lil&#8217; guy, to boot.</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Gligar will repeatedly charge at an opponent at lightning speed from random angles, hitting them away in the process. Each time it charges, its attack increases in strength!</p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/gligar2.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>A solid hit at first&#8230;</strong></p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/gligar3.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>&#8230;but later on, a massive one!</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">If someone gets hit several times in a row, they&#8217;re likely to get KO&#8217;d. There is a catch, though: if Gligar&#8217;s attack is avoided, it stops the barrage entirely. Do whatever you can to make sure the opponent keeps getting hit!</p>
]]></content:encoded>
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Phase 8</title>
		<link>http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/stages/phase-8-2</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 27 Dec 2013 07:48:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[SSF2 DOJO Team]]></dc:creator>
				<category><![CDATA[Stages]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/?p=4985</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Phase 8 continues the tradition of similar stages from the Metroid universe in previous Smash Bros. games. This can mean only one thing: Hot hot HOT! Find refuge in higher ground. Lava will periodically rise up from below and force you to get away or risk getting burned. However, that&#8217;s not the only thing that [&#8230;]]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/phase8full.png" height="275px" /></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Phase 8 continues the tradition of similar stages from the Metroid universe in previous Smash Bros. games. This can mean only one thing:</p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/phase8-5.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>Hot hot HOT!</strong></p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/phase8-6.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>Find refuge in higher ground.</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Lava will periodically rise up from below and force you to get away or risk getting burned. However, that&#8217;s not the only thing that you have to look out for.</p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/Phase8-3.png" height="220px" /><br />
<strong>More lava!? Ouch!</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A lava flow will create a wall down the middle of the screen! There&#8217;s only one way to get through.</p>
<p><img alt="" src="http://ssfdojo.mcleodgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/phase8-2.png" height="220px" /><br />
<b>I hope this glass holds&#8230;</b></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Siding will appear between the two platforms in the center of the stage, allowing you to get past the lava. You can also use this as an early warning sign that the lava is coming, as it will appear several seconds beforehand.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It would be easy to avoid all this lava if you were left to your own devices. Your opponents are probably going to do their best to hit you into it, though.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">
]]></content:encoded>
